# TLS termination for the eBPCO API. API_HOST comes from deploy/.env via the
# compose file; Caddy obtains and renews a Let's Encrypt certificate for it
# automatically, which is the whole reason Caddy and not nginx: there is no
# certbot cron to forget.
#
# Requires: an A record for API_HOST pointing at this host, and ports 80 and
# 443 open. The first request after `up` may take a few seconds while the
# certificate is issued.
#
# reverse_proxy sets X-Forwarded-For and X-Forwarded-Proto on its own; the
# API trusts them because TRUST_PROXY=true, and it is safe to because nothing
# but this proxy can reach api:3000 (see the compose file: no published port).
# HSTS is set by the API itself (security.ts), not duplicated here.
{$API_HOST} {
	reverse_proxy api:3000
}
